# Delivery Guardrails

- Implement only the requested scope; do not scaffold new app setup, tooling, or dependencies unless explicitly asked.
- Avoid over-engineering: prefer clear, minimal solutions over speculative abstractions.
- Do not introduce charts, advanced visualizations, or heavy business-rule engines unless explicitly requested.
- Keep UI behavior predictable and accessible; favor simple dashboard interactions over novelty patterns.
- Maintain consistency with existing stack choices and project conventions before proposing alternatives.
- When trade-offs exist, choose the option that is easiest for the team to maintain and test.
